# Opening a JES scene
@scenario tutorial_lesson_17
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: I built a small panel in JES. You can visit it from my script and come back here when you're done.
ginger: Open the example below. Press Enter or Esc to return. Its source is scripts/scenes/panel.jes.
> Open the example scene -> visit
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label visit
[jes push scripts/scenes/panel.jes label check]
@label check
ginger: Where would you edit a JES panel?
> In the .jes scene that owns it. -> correct
> In the speaker declaration. -> retry
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: VNS controls story flow. JES owns the entities in its scene. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: VNS controls story flow. JES owns the entities in its scene.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_17]
[flag tutorial_done_17]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_5]
